            <ArticleTitle>[Complaints after fractures of the os calcis-significance of the peroneal tendons (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>95-104</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In complaints following fractures of the os calcis a peroneal synovitis arisen from side plate dislocation has a share. This alteration may be securely diagnosed by making tenosynoviagrams. The side plate that healed in a bad position must be chiselled off subperiostally so that the complaints be stopped. A suitable first treatment may have prevented a large portion of after-complaints.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
